iter_76: cross-swap success/refund preserves caller, refund, excess, and route fields.
iter_78/88: pay_vault/Vault StateInit, Router-only deposit, stored amount, carry/destroy, and replay behavior.
iter_90/99: pay_to custom-payload dispatch and carry modes preserve fixed amounts/destinations.
iter_213: pay_vault StateInit bounce/fee-stranding boundary has no external forced path.
iter_258: Vault schema, exact deposit/withdraw, and carry/destroy lifecycle duplicate.

Command:
rg -n --no-heading -i 'swap_refund|referral|pay_vault|pay_to|CARRY_ALL_BALANCE|NORMAL|storage::save|reserve.*catch|pool.*referral|vault.*state_init' CHAIN_HYPOTHESIS_TABLE.md iter_*/STATUS.yaml

Conclusion: DD1 is a narrowed duplicate of Pool swap catch rollback plus referral pay_vault/Vault delivery and Router pay_to carry audits; referral delivery failure is liveness/ledger handling, not an external selected-asset theft path.
